**The picture is complete:**
- ICMP (ping) from Office A → Office B is explicitly **accepted** (first rule matches)
- **All other traffic** (TCP/UDP — HTTP, application sessions, etc.) from Office A → Office B hits the second rule and is **silently dropped**
- This explains why PC1 can ping colleagues and reach the internet (different subnets/paths) but any TCP connection to srv1 just "times out" — the SYN is dropped at the distribution layer with no RST

This is a confirmed ACL fault on **dswa1** and **dswa2**.

